    "presentation": {
      "chief_complaint": "Hip fracture",
      "hpi": "An 87-year-old man with atrial fibrillation falls and is admitted with a right femoral-neck fracture. Warfarin is held for fixation. Admission INR is 2.6 and the day-of-surgery INR is 1.3. Enoxaparin 40 mg subcutaneously once daily is used while the INR is below 2 and is stopped at discharge because the INR is 2.1. Warfarin 5 mg orally once daily was resumed the evening after surgery. Hemoglobin is 11.4 g/dL before surgery, 9.0 g/dL after, and 10.1 g/dL at discharge, without transfusion. Lisinopril and metformin continue. Creatinine is 1.0 mg/dL. Anticoagulation clinic is in 7 days.",
